---
// src/components/SocialScraping.astro
---

<section class="py-12" data-animate-on-scroll>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto glass-panel p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 shadow-md">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-start gap-6">
        
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 text-brand-blue flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 shadow-2xs">
          <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 20l4-16m4 4l4 4-4 4M6 16l-4-4 4-4" />
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3 text-center sm:text-left">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center sm:justify-start gap-2">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-slate">Engineering Behind the Data</h3>
            <span class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 border border-slate-200">
              Python &bull; Selenium Pipeline
            </span>
          </div>

          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The <em>Valued Colleagues & Thinkers</em> ranking is powered by an automated Python data extraction pipeline. Using headless browser telemetry, it analyzes my LinkedIn activity and engagement counts to calculate transparent interaction affinities. It's a small demonstration of treating professional networking with the same analytical rigor as development economics.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>